{"version":"0.1","documentType":"opinion","source":{"kind":"lrb_html","caseId":"2017_03442","path":"opinions/coa/2017/2017_03442.htm","publicationStatus":"published"},"header":{"title":"People v Smalling","slipOpinion":"2017 NY Slip Op 03442 [29 NY3d 981]","officialCitation":null,"court":"Court of Appeals","decisionDate":null},"appearances":[],"opinions":[{"kind":"majority","author":null,"label":null,"joiners":[],"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"{**29 NY3d at 982}"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"{**29 NY3d at 982}"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Memorandum."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The order of the Appellate Division should be reversed and a new trial ordered."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Although we reject defendant's contention that the evidence presented at trial did not support a charge of constructive possession, we nevertheless conclude that defendant is entitled to a new trial. The trial court erred in that it agreed to the People's request at the charge "},{"type":"text","text":"conference not to charge the jury on constructive possession, but then ultimately provided a constructive possession charge to the jury, resulting in prejudice to defendant ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see"}]},{"type":"text","text":" CPL 300.10 [4]; "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"People v Greene"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 75 NY2d 875, 876-877 [1990]). Under the unique circumstances of this case, the error is not harmless ("},{"type":"link","href":"../2005/2005_02021.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"cf. People v Nevins"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 16 AD3d 1046"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 1047 [4th Dept 2005], "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"lv denied"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 4 NY3d 889 [2005], "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"cert denied"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 548 US 911 [2006])."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Chief Judge DiFiore and Judges Rivera, Stein, Fahey, Garcia and Wilson concur."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Order reversed and a new trial ordered, in a memorandum."}],"provenance":{"startLine":7,"endLine":19}}]}],"footnotes":[],"disposition":null,"renderingHints":{"hasOfficialPageMarkers":true,"hasAppearances":false,"hasFootnotes":false,"hasSeparateOpinions":false},"debug":{"diagnostics":[]}}
